# Phase 1 — a customer rates a resolved ticket

Makes work: a signed-in customer rates a resolved ticket of their own organisation
1–5; a second rating, a bad score, a non-resolved ticket, or another org's ticket is
refused; a score of 1–2 queues an email to the assigned agent.

Check that demonstrates it: `node --test test/tickets.test.js` passes, including the
new cases below.

Blocked by: none.

## Context

- `src/store.js` — the in-memory store; `tickets`/`messages` are `Map`s keyed by
  ticket id. Ratings follow the same shape: one `ratings` `Map`, keyed by ticket id
  (a ticket has at most one rating, so a map entry, not an array).
- `src/portal.js` — everything a customer does, gated through `getMyTicket` (returns
  `null` for a missing ticket or another org's ticket — reused as-is here).
- `src/tickets.js:38-44` (`reopenTicket`) — the existing pattern for "validate, guard
  the notify call on a truthy agent id" that this phase mirrors.
- `src/notify.js:6-9` (`notifyAgent`) — throws if called without an agent id; this is
  exactly the crash the Phase-1 unassigned-ticket test below guards against.
- `docs/specs/csat-rating.md` requirements 1–4 and their acceptance criteria.

## Files

- Modify `src/store.js`: add `addRating`/`getRating` to the object `createStore`
  returns.
- Modify `src/portal.js`: add `rateTicket`, require `notifyAgent` from `./notify`.
- Modify `test/tickets.test.js`: append the rating test cases (this file already
  mixes `tickets.js` and `portal.js` tests, e.g. `reply`/`getMyTicket` below).

## Steps

- [ ] 1. Add the new tests to `test/tickets.test.js`, appended after the last test:

  ```js
  test('a customer rates a resolved ticket of their organisation, and the rating is stored with its score and time', () => {
    const store = createStore();
    const t = portal.openTicket(store, acme, { subject: 'Printer', body: 'x' });
    assignTicket(store, t.id, 41);
    resolveTicket(store, t.id, 41, { now: at(1) });
    const rating = portal.rateTicket(store, acme, t.id, 4, { now: at(2) });
    assert.equal(rating.score, 4);
    assert.equal(rating.ratedAt, at(2).toISOString());
  });

  test('a score that is not a whole number from 1 to 5 is refused', () => {
    const store = createStore();
    const t = portal.openTicket(store, acme, { subject: 'Printer', body: 'x' });
    assignTicket(store, t.id, 41);
    resolveTicket(store, t.id, 41, { now: at(1) });
    assert.throws(() => portal.rateTicket(store, acme, t.id, 0), /score must be a whole number from 1 to 5/);
    assert.throws(() => portal.rateTicket(store, acme, t.id, 6), /score must be a whole number from 1 to 5/);
    assert.throws(() => portal.rateTicket(store, acme, t.id, 3.5), /score must be a whole number from 1 to 5/);
  });

  test('rating an open or pending ticket is refused', () => {
    const store = createStore();
    const t = portal.openTicket(store, acme, { subject: 'Printer', body: 'x' });
    assert.throws(() => portal.rateTicket(store, acme, t.id, 4), /cannot rate a open ticket/);
    store.updateTicket(t.id, { status: STATUS.PENDING });
    assert.throws(() => portal.rateTicket(store, acme, t.id, 4), /cannot rate a pending ticket/);
  });

  test('a second rating of the same ticket is refused, and the first stays as it was', () => {
    const store = createStore();
    const t = portal.openTicket(store, acme, { subject: 'Printer', body: 'x' });
    assignTicket(store, t.id, 41);
    resolveTicket(store, t.id, 41, { now: at(1) });
    portal.rateTicket(store, acme, t.id, 4, { now: at(2) });
    assert.throws(() => portal.rateTicket(store, acme, t.id, 1, { now: at(3) }), /already been rated/);
    assert.equal(store.getRating(t.id).score, 4);
  });

  test('a customer of another organisation gets the same answer as for a ticket that does not exist', () => {
    const store = createStore();
    const t = portal.openTicket(store, acme, { subject: 'Printer', body: 'x' });
    assignTicket(store, t.id, 41);
    resolveTicket(store, t.id, 41, { now: at(1) });
    assert.equal(portal.rateTicket(store, globex, t.id, 4), null);
    assert.equal(portal.rateTicket(store, acme, 999, 4), null);
  });

  test('a score of 1 or 2 notifies the assigned agent; a score of 3 does not', () => {
    const store = createStore();
    drain();
    const low = portal.openTicket(store, acme, { subject: 'Printer', body: 'x' });
    assignTicket(store, low.id, 41);
    resolveTicket(store, low.id, 41, { now: at(1) });
    portal.rateTicket(store, acme, low.id, 2, { now: at(2) });
    assert.deepEqual(drain().map((m) => [m.to, m.event.type]), [['agent:41', 'ticket_rated_low']]);

    const ok = portal.openTicket(store, acme, { subject: 'Invoice', body: 'x' });
    assignTicket(store, ok.id, 41);
    resolveTicket(store, ok.id, 41, { now: at(1) });
    portal.rateTicket(store, acme, ok.id, 3, { now: at(2) });
    assert.deepEqual(drain(), []);
  });

  test('a low score on a resolved but unassigned ticket is stored without notifying anyone', () => {
    const store = createStore();
    drain();
    const t = portal.openTicket(store, acme, { subject: 'Printer', body: 'x' });
    resolveTicket(store, t.id, 41, { now: at(1) });
    const rating = portal.rateTicket(store, acme, t.id, 1, { now: at(2) });
    assert.equal(rating.score, 1);
    assert.deepEqual(drain(), []);
  });
  ```

