# Phase 3 — `assignee_id` becomes `owner_id` (COUNCIL)

**Needs your explicit sign-off before this is built** — not just the recommendation
below. It touches `exports/tickets.json`, read by finance's reporting job outside
this repo (`src/jobs/export-tickets.js:3`), which this repo cannot verify is safe to
cut over in one step.

Makes work: every in-repo reader uses `owner_id`; the export keeps writing the old
`assignee_id` key too, so finance's job keeps working unmodified; the glossary says
"Owner" instead of "Assignee."

Check that demonstrates it: `node --test` is green; `exports/tickets.json` (via the
test in step 3) has both `owner_id` and `assignee_id` with the same value.

Blocked by: Phase 1 (`src/portal.js`'s `rateTicket` reads `t.assignee_id`; this phase
moves that read to `t.owner_id`).

## Scope decision (plan.md decision 4)

This is an **expand only**, not expand-migrate-contract. The in-repo rename is a
single atomic step (small blast radius — `src/tickets.js`, `src/portal.js`,
`docs/glossary.md`, two test files — and nothing here can be only-half-migrated
without breaking the suite immediately, so it doesn't need its own
sub-phases). The one external reader is handled by dual-writing the export, and
**contract (dropping the legacy `assignee_id` key from the export) is not in this
plan** — it waits on finance confirming they've moved to `owner_id`. Record that
confirmation in a handoff note when it happens; removing the legacy key is then a
one-line follow-up, not a new investigation.

