===== docs/plans/261006-1500-csat-rating/plan.md =====
# CSAT rating — implementation plan

Spec: `docs/specs/csat-rating.md` (approved, Mai Do, 2026-01-12).

## Goal

A customer rates a resolved ticket 1–5 from the portal (once, own org only), a low
score (1–2) emails the agent, a nightly job writes a per-agent weekly summary, and
`assignee_id` becomes `owner_id` everywhere.

## Phases

| # | Phase | File | Status | Blocked by | Gate |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Rate a ticket | `phase-01-rate-ticket.md` | not started | none | ACT |
| 2 | Weekly summary job | `phase-02-weekly-summary.md` | not started | Phase 1 | ACT |
| 3 | `assignee_id` → `owner_id` | `phase-03-owner-id-rename.md` | not started | Phase 1 | **COUNCIL** |

Phase 1 is the thinnest end-to-end slice (store → portal → test). Phase 2 widens it
with a nightly report over the same data. Phase 3 is independent of 1–2 in content
but is sequenced last because it touches the export every other phase's tests read,
and it needs the user's sign-off before it's built, not just a recommendation.

## Decisions needing your sign-off (answered with a recommendation; confirm or correct)

1. **Weekly-window boundary.** The spec pins only "eight days old is not counted."
   Is a rating exactly 7 days old in or out? **Recommended: out** (`age >= 7 days`
   drops it), matching the direction `close-resolved.js`/`purge-closed.js` already use
   for their day-count cutoffs (`src/jobs/close-resolved.js:11`,
   `src/jobs/purge-closed.js:14`). Phase 2's test avoids the exact-7-day edge case so
   it stays correct either way; revisit if you want it pinned differently.
2. **Attributing a rating to an agent.** Snapshot the agent on the rating itself at
   rating time (`agentId`), or look up the ticket's current `assignee_id`/`owner_id`
   at report time? **Recommended: snapshot.** `assignTicket` (`src/tickets.js:25`)
   only refuses on a `closed` ticket, so a resolved-and-rated ticket can be
   reassigned afterward; a live lookup would silently re-attribute history to the
   new agent.
3. **Unassigned ticket, low score.** `resolveTicket` never requires an assignee, so
   a resolved-but-unassigned ticket can be rated 1–2. `notifyAgent` throws without an
   agent id (`src/notify.js:7`). **Recommended: skip the email, store the rating**,
   mirroring the existing guard in `reopenTicket` (`src/tickets.js:42`,
   `if (t.assignee_id && ...)`).
